The two records `records.py` reads, added to each build for the instrumented
walks and to neither for the readings.

Runs 30 and 31 needed no patch: their probe sites are in the tree, kept there so
a later walk can read them again. These two are not, and the reason to ship the
diff rather than describe it is that the run turns on them — `guard` at the
instant a stale page lands is the difference between #540 firing and not, and
nothing already in the tree records it.

`git apply` one of them, build with `VITE_PROBE=1 npm run tauri build
-- --no-bundle`, and walk with `IRCX_PROBE` naming a file, which `wedge.sh`
always sets. Both hunks are compiled out of a build that does not ask for the
probe, so neither is a difference between the instrumented binary and the plain
one anywhere but here.

